# finish/filigree: T5-T6 filigree on P (STYLE_P2 27.3; P2C_CONTRACTS 3b; LADDER-FINISH, ladder slice i3). i3: the
# cloak's back badge (9x10, 7x8, 9x12: a lobed oak leaf, Jade's cloud curl, the Imperial laurel wreath, a Fjordfolk knot;
# gold LINES on the cloth with a dark-gold relief, not chased), the heater's field gilded with one leaf hanging from the
# boss (i2's chased mottle read as noise), breastplate sprigs of 2-3 px instead of a solid gold block. Gold drawn as
# SHAPES (every gold pixel touches another; no scattered dots): O metal2 at the plane's own step so the gold follows the
# plate's light, * metal2 4 the lit point at a scroll's end, N metal2 one step under the plane (knotwork's under-crossing).
# One drawing a people, keys <motif><w>x<h>, FIT-centred on the part's P box (the largest view that fits): oak = the
# Heartland (sprigs with acorns on a brow band, the oak tree on a shield's field, a sprig pair over the chest gem, one
# leaf on a pauldron), clouds = Jade's cloud scrolls, laurel = the Imperial laurel wreath, knot = Fjordfolk / Highland
# knotwork. The resolver passes the maker people's motif (oak when a people has none). `rest`: the periodic fallback.
# Generated by LADDER-FINISH's gen_finish.py.
use person
body adult
role overlay finish.filigree
legend * metal2 4
tags tile overlay fit
on-region P

